.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Christiaan Huygens&#x27; 1690 construction treats every point of an advancing wavefront as the source of a new spherical secondary wavelet; the envelope of all those wavelets a moment later reconstructs the propagated wavefront. angular_spectrum_propagate realizes exactly this modern form of the picture. The scalar field U_0(x,y) right after the aperture is decomposed into its plane-wave (angular) spectrum by a 2D Fourier transform; each plane-wave component, labeled by transverse spatial frequency (f_x,f_y), is a secondary wavelet that advances rigidly along z picking up phase e^{ik_z z}; re-synthesizing (inverse Fourier transform) sums the interference of all these wavelets at the new plane:">

